the transaction qualifies for the section 4(a)(6) exemption
===========================================================

1 way this can be satisfied.

  1. (a) Exemption. An issuer may offer or sell securities in reliance on section 4(a)(6) of the Securities Act of 1933, provided that: issuer is eligible OF issuer offering is within the offering limit OF offering investor is within the investment limit OF investor, amount intermediary obligations are met OF arrangement disclosure requirements are met OF filing, offering
